          "message_id": "e7b31493-2bd0-48ce-9726-d17d2fb3e794",
          "content": "Here's how to add the Pages API to your app:\n\n**1. Go to your App Dashboard**\n- Visit [developers.facebook.com/apps](https://developers.facebook.com/apps)\n- Click on your app\n\n**2. Add Pages API Product**\n- In the left sidebar, scroll down and click **\"Add Product\"**\n- Find **\"Facebook Login for Business\"** — click **Set Up**\n- Also look for **\"Pages API\"** and click **Set Up**\n\n> If you don't see \"Pages API\" directly, it's accessed through **Facebook Login** permissions — not a separate product.\n\n**3. Set Up Facebook Login**\n- After adding Facebook Login, go to its **Settings**\n- Under **Valid OAuth Redirect URIs** add: `https://localhost` (for testing)\n\n**4. Get Permissions for Pages**\nYou need these specific permissions:\n| Permission | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `pages_manage_posts` | Create/publish posts |\n| `pages_read_engagement` | Read page data |\n| `pages_show_list` | See list of your pages |\n\n**5. Use Graph API Explorer to Test**\n- Go to [developers.facebook.com/tools/explorer](https://developers.facebook.com/tools/explorer)\n- Select your app from the dropdown\n- Click **\"Generate Access Token\"**\n- Check the permissions above\n- Click **\"Generate\"** and log in with your Facebook account\n\n**6. Find Your Page ID**\n- In the Explorer, type `me/accounts` in the query box\n- Click **\"Submit\"**\n- You'll see your pages listed with their `id` and `access_token`\n\nThat `access_token` in the response is your **Page Access Token** — save it!\n\n---\n\nOnce you have the token and page ID, share them with me (or add them to `.env`) and I'll build out the Phase 3 publishing feature. Want me to show you what that code will look like?"
